      fill="none"
      stroke="currentColor"
      strokeWidth="2"
      strokeLinecap="round"
    />
  </g>
</svg>
```
Rationale: the body's top end is the straight cut edge between (25,4) and (28,8); the stem now starts at that edge's midpoint (26.2,6.3) and hooks up-right, so it visually grows out of the body. Remove the `banana-stem` className (no longer used anywhere; grep to confirm).

Then measure the real bounding box of `.banana-shape` in a browser (Playwright, `el.getBBox()` on the `<g>` in a rendered page, or a tiny throwaway HTML file) and report cx, cy of the bbox in viewBox user units. Use those values as the transform-origin below (round to one decimal). If the stem visibly doesn't touch the body in a screenshot zoomed at 8x, nudge the stem's start point along the cut edge until it does and report the final `d`.

### 2. app/styles/motion.css
a) Replace the block at lines 351-366 (`.banana-loading svg`, `.banana-loading .banana-stem`, `@keyframes banana-swing`) with:

```css
.banana-loading .banana-shape {
  transform-box: view-box;
  transform-origin: <cx>px <cy>px;
  animation: banana-spin 1.5s linear infinite;
}
@keyframes banana-spin {
  0% {
    transform: rotate(0deg);
    animation-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0.65, 0, 0.35, 1);
  }
  58% {
    transform: rotate(372deg);
    animation-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1);
  }
  70% {
    transform: rotate(360deg);
  }
  100% {
    transform: rotate(360deg);
  }
}
```
